# Compose defaults for the FinCore dev stack.
#
# No secrets and no deployment specifics live here (AGENTS.md hard rule 8) — only local dev
# selections, the same posture compose.yaml already takes with its throwaway dev credentials.
# Override anything in your shell or a personal .env.local.

# ── Event backbone: pick exactly one ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The backbone is a runtime choice, not a code dependency (ADR 0005). Kafka and RabbitMQ are both
# first-class, supported options — this is open source and you are free to run either. They are
# mutually exclusive, and each sits behind its own compose profile, so only the one you choose is
# ever provisioned; the two never come up together.
#
#   Kafka  (default, recommended): docker compose up
#   RabbitMQ                      : COMPOSE_PROFILES=rabbit FINCORE_EVENTS_BROKER=rabbit docker compose up
#
# Kafka is recommended because it is a durable log — Compliance and Reporting can replay history,
# and a consumer added later still receives earlier events. RabbitMQ is the right pick when your
# consumers only react to what is happening now.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=kafka,edge
FINCORE_EVENTS_BROKER=kafka
